{"id":"0827b9c2-bb14-42cf-80c1-f7acfe34a135","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6e5f06658585bd5f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/playground-link.ts","baseline":{"blob":"22140f25524f6e7da002be0fea349cd32fc5b39c","start":0,"end":32},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","LZString","from","\"","lz-string","\""]},"context":{"after":"41c0430da5e0222e"}},"payload":{"text":"TypeScript Playground links, opened as projects — and written, to share one. Swap the host of any playground link for\nours and the same hash opens here as a real workspace. The shell decodes it (it owns the URL) and hands the files to the\napp as a project load, the same way a GitHub repo arrives. Share writes the workspace back out as a v2 link, which the\nplayground itself opens too.\n\nThe formats, as the playground writes them:\n• `#code/v2/<lz>` (Playground v2): lz-string JSON `{ version, files: { \"/workspace/…\": text }, activeFile, selection }`\n— a whole project, tsconfig.json included.\n• `#code/<lz>` (the classic playground): one file's source, lz-string compressed; its compiler options ride the query\nstring (`?target=4&strict=false`), as the ones that differ from the playground's defaults.\n• `#src=<text>`: one file's source, URI-encoded.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:51.990Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:51.990Z"}
{"id":"276f65c7-424f-41de-879a-cc57d59e239c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"4b7cee403db72124","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/playground-link.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c845440e2f2e6a3daf7b0e4fc1aeb770a79cb4b5","start":6977,"end":7145},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","PlaygroundSelection","{","\"","positionLineNumber","\"",":","number",";","\"","positionColumn","\"",":","number",";","\"","selectionStartLineNumber","\"",":","number",";","\"","selectionStartColumn","\"",":","number",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"4fb76c4c682f58dc","after":"f40a8e7633e668b3"}},"payload":{"text":"Where the cursor was, as the playground records it: Monaco's 1-based lines and columns.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:31.744Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:31.744Z"}
